WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.860
In a dish, the experimenter decides where support is lost.

2
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:09.080
In the animal, who decides?

3
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:14.710
Many sympathetic neurons send branches toward targets that make NGF.

4
00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:16.710
The branches compete.

5
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.690
When NGF is limited, a branch that wins enough is stabilized.

6
00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:25.090
One left with too little is weakened and removed.

7
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.620
Two receptors matter.

8
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:30.440
TrkA is the NGF receptor.

9
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.040
p75 binds all neurotrophins, including BDNF.

10
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:39.363
One axon has strong TrkA signalling, the other weak.

11
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:43.263
BDNF is present. Which axon goes?

12
00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:57.367
The weak one. On axons with weak TrkA signalling, BDNF acting through p75 caused

13
00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.367
degeneration.

14
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.390
Axons with strong TrkA signalling were protected.

15
00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.390
And the winning neurons made the BDNF.

16
00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.573
So a winner does more than take the NGF.

17
00:01:09.513 --> 00:01:11.893
It also sends a signal that removes the loser.

18
00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:21.347
The neurotrophic hypothesis lesson showed the same winner-removes-loser idea for

19
00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.027
whole neurons. Here it works on axons.

20
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:28.677
So how does an axon come apart after NGF is withdrawn?

21
00:01:29.677 --> 00:01:30.677
Not all at once.

22
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.220
First, the axon waits through a long latent phase.

23
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.160
It looks nearly normal.

24
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:40.153
Late in latency, swellings called spheroids appear.

25
00:01:41.193 --> 00:01:42.293
Calcium gathers in them.

26
00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:44.657
Then the spheroids rupture.

27
00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:47.950
Then the axon fragments.

28
00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:50.370
That is the catastrophic phase.

29
00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:56.503
Two receptors split the work.

30
00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.063
p75 is needed for spheroids to form.

31
00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:07.027
DR6 is needed for the catastrophic degeneration that medium from deprived axons

32
00:02:07.027 --> 00:02:08.027
speeds up.

33
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:13.200
The Deppmann laboratory's model is that spheroids gate the step from waiting to

34
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.580
catastrophe. It is not yet a settled mechanism.

35
00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.270
Where support is lost decides what is lost.

36
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.410
In a contest, the winner helps decide too.
